        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "Draft: add commands list and inspect inventory",
        "body": "## Summary\n\nAdds a read-only operator/developer command inventory:\n\n```text\nopenclaw commands list [--json|--markdown] [--plugin-descriptors]\nopenclaw commands inspect <command-path...> [--json|--markdown] [--plugin-descriptors]\n```\n\nThis is the recommended initial implementation from [Command Catalog RFC #32](https://github.com/openclaw/rfcs/pull/32). It joins command information OpenClaw already owns so compliance, diagnostics, documentation, policy tooling, and future scoped prompt consumers do not each rebuild the same registry joins.\n\n## Scope\n\n`commands list` joins existing command-owned sources:\n\n- static CLI descriptors\n- command routes and routed operations\n- the current Commander tree\n- opt-in plugin CLI descriptors\n- caller-supplied node command declarations\n\n`commands inspect` hydrates the requested lazy core/sub-CLI group, resolves runtime aliases, and joins exact command records with inherited route and routed-operation metadata.\n\nThis draft does not add ownerless tool adapters, aggregate audit/test/summary commands, prompt generation, generated docs, or a new execution path. Node records are supported in the object model but no live `node.list` / `node.describe` bridge is claimed yet.\n\n## Plugin contract and failure behavior\n\nPlugin descriptors may optionally report `effectProfile`, `commandExposure`, and `hidden`. Their values, defaults, and non-enforcement semantics are documented in `docs/plugins/sdk-overview.md` with an external-plugin example.\n\nWhen `--plugin-descriptors` is requested, loader exceptions or error-level plugin diagnostics now fail the command. They cannot produce an apparently valid incomplete inventory. Warnings remain visible without invalidating successful results.\n\n## Existing Gateway surface\n\nOpenClaw already has Gateway RPC `commands.list` for agent-facing chat/native/skill/plugin commands. This CLI adds an operator/developer inventory; it does not replace or change the Gateway RPC. Future convergence remains an explicit RFC decision.\n\n## Review layers\n\n- [PR1: commands list](https://github.com/giodl73-repo/openclaw/pull/24)\n- [PR2: commands inspect and ClawSweeper hardening](https://github.com/giodl73-repo/openclaw/pull/25)\n- [Optional PR3: scoped prompt projection](https://github.com/giodl73-repo/openclaw/pull/26)\n\n## Real behavior proof\n\nExact head: `90a7b1ca2b`\n\nCore-only inventory, using an isolated state directory:\n\n```text\nschemaVersion=1\ncommandDescriptors=61\nruntimeCommands=26\npluginCommands=0\n```\n\nOpt-in plugin inventory, also isolated:\n\n```json\n{\"schemaVersion\":1,\"commandDescriptors\":61,\"runtimeCommands\":26,\"pluginCommands\":3,\"pluginIds\":\"browser:browser,canvas:nodes canvas,memory-core:memory\"}\n```\n\nControlled plugin registration failure:\n\n```json\n{\"exitCode\":1,\"stdoutBytes\":0,\"errorMatched\":true}\n```\n\nThe failure fixture throws during plugin registration. The command emits no JSON document and exits nonzero with `Failed to load plugin CLI descriptor metadata` on stderr.\n\n## Validation\n\n- 44 focused inventory tests from the promoted PR1+PR2 stack\n- latest hardening rerun: 10 focused CLI/metadata tests passed\n- source execution proved core-only, plugin-enabled, and plugin-failure paths\n- `git diff --check`\n- clean final Codex review after the ClawSweeper fixes\n\nThe full local core TypeScript runner did not complete within two five-minute attempts on this worktree; it emitted no diagnostics. Focused Vitest compilation and runtime source execution passed.\n\n## Feedback requested\n\nIs `openclaw commands` the right initial public surface, with broader consumers added only after the command inventory contract is accepted?",
        "branch": "user/giodl/cli-catalog-review-hardening",
